    .build();

HiveSink.Builder<String> builder = HiveSink.forStreaming(kafkaStream, hiveOptions);
kafkaStream.addSink(builder.build());
```

4. Configuration and Execution

- Ensure all necessary dependencies are added to your project.
- Configure the Flink cluster and job parameters.
- Deploy and run the Flink jobs.

Considerations:

1. Ensure version compatibility between Flink, Kafka, and Hive.
2. Adjust data transformation logic based on actual requirements.
3. Consider data consistency and fault tolerance; checkpoint mechanisms may be needed.
4. Monitor the entire data pipeline and set up appropriate alert mechanisms.
5. Address data privacy and security by ensuring sensitive data is properly protected.

This solution provides a scalable, real-time data synchronization approach. Leveraging Flink's streaming capabilities and Kafka's message queue enables high throughput and low-latency data synchronization. Additionally, this architecture offers good decoupling, making the system easier to maintain and expand.

